//arxiv.org/abs/2302.00883", "problem": "", "method": "Supply a target object bounding box for simulated sitting, lying down, or box carrying.", "contribution": "", "gap": "", "limitations": "", "sourceExcerpts": {}, "datasets": {"entries": [{"name": "SAMP", "page": 3, "excerpt": "Synthesizing Physical Character-Scene Interactions • 3 experts [Eigen et al. 2014; Jacobs et al. 1991] to synthesize object in- teraction behaviors, such as sitting and carrying. SAMP [Hassan et al. 2021] avoids the need for phase labels by training an auto-regressive cVAE [Diederik and Welling 2014; Sohn et al. 2015] using scheduled sampling [Bengio et al. 2015]. Instead of manually labelling a single phase f", "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.00883", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}], "status": "Dataset names found in source data/method passages; inspect the cited passage for their exact use."}, "readStatus": "Demonstration described in the prior reading list", "evidence": [], "origin": "assets/directions/xr-research-reading-list.md — Papers in the final plot", "figureSource": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.00883", "figureCredit": "", "tags": {}}, {"id": "map-generatinghumaninteractionmotionsinsceneswithtextcontrol", "images": [{"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-generatinghumaninteractionmotionsinsceneswithtextcontrol-410976a2c990.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "locator": "Figure 1, PDF page 1", "kind": "Teaser figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111110111111111111111011110000011111000000000000111110111100000001111001110000000111100001000000011111000000000001111100000000000011111000000100011111100000010001111110000001100111111000000000001111100000000000111110000000000011111111000000001", "width": 697, "height": 398, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-generatinghumaninteractionmotionsinsceneswithtextcontrol-0ff70de3e548.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "locator": "Figure 2, PDF page 5", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111111111111111111111100111110110000001100111001100111111111100110001101111100010000110110010001001000000000000000100000000000100010001000000010000000000010000000000000001100110001111111111111111110000111001100111111111111111111111111111111111", "width": 557, "height": 162, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-generatinghumaninteractionmotionsinsceneswithtextcontrol-aae285b45e82.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "locator": "Figure 3, PDF page 7", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111011111111111111110111111111111000011000001111110000010000011111000001000001111100000000000111100000000000011110000000000001111000000000000111110000010000011111000001000001111110010110011111111111111111111", "width": 930, "height": 387, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-generatinghumaninteractionmotionsinsceneswithtextcontrol-1505bf75fc5a.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "locator": "Figure 4, PDF page 10", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111100111111111111100011101111111110001110111111110000111011111111010011101111111100000100101001110000010000100111100001000010011110000100001001111000111110110111100011111111011110001111001101111000111100110111100011110011011110001100000001111101110100111", "width": 455, "height": 168, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}], "title": "Generating Human Interaction Motions in Scenes with Text Control", "year": 2024, "venue": "ECCV 2024", "group": "direction", "image": "", "url": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "problem": "Source abstract: We present TeSMo, a text-controlled scene-aware motion generation method based on denoising diffusion models. Previous text- to-motion methods focus on characters in isolation without consider- ing scenes due to the limited availability of datasets that include mo- tion, text descriptions, and interactive scenes. Our approach begins with pre-training a scene-agnostic text-to-motion diffusion model, emphasiz- ing…", "method": "TeSMo generates sitting from a goal pelvis pose and chair geometry, and walks to a supplied floor goal around obstacles.", "contribution": "", "gap": "", "limitations": "", "sourceExcerpts": {"abstractExcerpt": "We present TeSMo, a text-controlled scene-aware motion generation method based on denoising diffusion models. Previous text- to-motion methods focus on characters in isolation without consider- ing scenes due to the limited availability of datasets that include mo- tion, text descriptions, and interactive scenes. Our approach begins with pre-training a scene-agnostic text-to-motion diffusion model, emphasiz- ing…", "abstractSource": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "abstractLocator": "Abstract, PDF opening pages"}, "datasets": {"entries": [{"name": "HumanML3D", "page": 2, "excerpt": "s with paired human-scene data that captures realistic interactions. First, we pre-train a text-conditioned diffusion model [36] on a diverse motion dataset with no objects (e.g., HumanML3D [7]), allowing it to learn a realistic motion prior and the correlation with text. We then fine-tune the", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}, {"name": "3D-FRONT", "page": 8, "excerpt": "scenes with corresponding text prompts. For this purpose, we create the Loco-3D- FRONT dataset by integrating locomotion sequences from HumanML3D into diverse 3D environments from 3D-FRONT [6]. Each motion is placed within a different scene with randomized initial translation and orientation, following the methodology outlined in [43], as depicted in Fig. 4(a). Additionally, we apply left-right mirroring to both th", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}, {"name": "SAMP", "page": 9, "excerpt": " the accuracy of hitting the final pelvis pose. Object representation. The base interaction diffusion model is first trained on a dataset of interaction motions from HumanML3D and SAMP [9] without any objects, which helps develop a strong prior on interaction movements driven by text prompts. Similar to navigation, we then augment the base model with a new object-aware transformer encoder and fine-tune this enc", "sourceUrl": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}], "status": "Dataset names found in source data/method passages; inspect the cited passage for their exact use."}, "readStatus": "Demonstration described in the prior reading list", "evidence": [], "origin": "assets/directions/xr-research-reading-list.md — Six additional papers in the earlier performance-revision plot", "figureSource": "https://www.ecva.net/papers/eccv_2024/papers_ECCV/papers/00549.pdf", "figureCredit": "", "tags": {}}, {"id": "map-autonomouscharactersceneinteractionsynthesisfromtextinstruction", "images": [{"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-autonomouscharactersceneinteractionsynthesisfromtextinstruction-9c4038114037.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "locator": "Figure 1, PDF page 1", "kind": "Teaser figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111001111110001111110111111100011111011110110100001001011000000000000101111110000000010011100010000000011000000000000001100000000011000110000000000000011000000000000001100000000000000110000000000000011111111111111111", "width": 1030, "height": 533, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-autonomouscharactersceneinteractionsynthesisfromtextinstruction-e5855741e705.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "locator": "Figure 2, PDF page 4", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111110111111111111111111011111111101001101111011111110110111111111111111011111111101001101111011111111110111111111000011001111110001001100100011000101110110000100011111010000110001111101100011000111110010001100011111111000110001000001100011111111011111111", "width": 1030, "height": 419, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-autonomouscharactersceneinteractionsynthesisfromtextinstruction-83675e2458a9.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "locator": "Figure 3, PDF page 5", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111000001111111111101000000101000011000000000000000100000000000000000000010000001010000011111111111111111111111111110111111111111110100011111111111000000000000000010000000000000000000000000000000000000101001010111000111111111111111111111111111", "width": 1030, "height": 345, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}, {"image": "../assets/paper-gallery/map-autonomouscharactersceneinteractionsynthesisfromtextinstruction-709b305eba49.jpg", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "locator": "Figure 4, PDF page 6", "kind": "Method / results figure", "fingerprint": "1111111111111111110000100000000110000000000000011000001000110001100001100000000010000000000000001111111110111111111111111111111111100011011111111100000000111010111001110100000011111111110000001111101111000000110100111100000011110011110000001111111111000000", "width": 498, "height": 372, "attribution": "Original paper authors"}], "title": "Autonomous Character-Scene Interaction Synthesis from Text Instruction", "year": 2024, "venue": "SIGGRAPH Asia 2024", "group": "objects", "image": "", "url": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "problem": "", "method": "LINGO generates multi-stage interactions from text, scene geometry and 3D goals, such as picking up an apple, sitting and eating it.", "contribution": "", "gap": "", "limitations": "Source limitations excerpt: (i) Our approach concentrates on body-level mo- tions, ignoring the intricate details of hand-level manipulation and facial expressions. (ii) Although quantitative results indicate that our method achieves superior scene awareness compared to existing techniques, it does not guarantee a perfect physical plausibility of the generated motions. (iii) We have not researched the generaliz- ability of…", "sourceExcerpts": {"limitationsExcerpt": "(i) Our approach concentrates on body-level mo- tions, ignoring the intricate details of hand-level manipulation and facial expressions. (ii) Although quantitative results indicate that our method achieves superior scene awareness compared to existing techniques, it does not guarantee a perfect physical plausibility of the generated motions. (iii) We have not researched the generaliz- ability of…", "limitationsSource": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "limitationsLocator": "Limitations section, PDF page 8"}, "datasets": {"entries": [{"name": "SAMP", "page": 3, "excerpt": "e a limited set of actions, such as sitting, lying, and locomotion. Later, researchers begin to employ MoCap equipment, including IMU-based and optic-based systems like VICON. The SAMP dataset [Hassan et al. 2021], for example, covers various sitting, lying down, walking, and running styles in a scene. Guzov et al. [2023] tracks human movements in large indoor scenes, including interactions with articulated ob-", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}, {"name": "BEHAVE", "page": 3, "excerpt": "e hu- man manipulation of small objects [Fan et al. 2023; Taheri et al. 2020] or interactions with large objects [Bhatnagar et al. 2022; Jiang et al. 2023; Zhang et al. 2022]. The BEHAVE dataset [Bhatnagar et al. 2022], for instance, contains long sequences of humans interact- ing with 20 types of large objects. The GRAB dataset [Taheri et al. 2020], on the other hand, focuses on full-body motions of small object", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}, {"name": "GRAB", "page": 3, "excerpt": "iang et al. 2023; Zhang et al. 2022]. The BEHAVE dataset [Bhatnagar et al. 2022], for instance, contains long sequences of humans interact- ing with 20 types of large objects. The GRAB dataset [Taheri et al. 2020], on the other hand, focuses on full-body motions of small object manipulation using hands. The CHAIRS [Jiang et al. 2023] and COUCH [Zhang et al. 2022] datasets specifically target human interactions ", "sourceUrl": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "role": "Source data passage; training/evaluation role not yet individually verified"}], "status": "Dataset names found in source data/method passages; inspect the cited passage for their exact use."}, "readStatus": "Demonstration described in the prior reading list", "evidence": [], "origin": "assets/directions/xr-research-reading-list.md — Six additional papers in the earlier performance-revision plot", "figureSource": "https://yzhu.io/publication/hoi2024siggraphasia/paper.pdf", "figureCredit": "", "tags": {}}, {"id": "map-reactivegazeduringlocomotioninnaturalenvironments", "images": [], "title": "Reactive Gaze during Locomotion in Natural Environments", "year": 2024, "venue": "SCA / Computer Graphics Forum 2024", "group": "direction", "image": "", "url": "https://doi.org/10.111